---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';

import shotWelcome from '../../../assets/guide/09-student-welcome.png';
import shotHome from '../../../assets/guide/10-student-home.png';
---

<GuideLayout
  slug="student-getting-started"
  title="Getting started"
  description="Setting up your Zengarden account, joining your school, and finding your way around."
  audience="For students"
  readingTime="3 min read"
>
  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">1</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Create your account</h2>
      <p>
        Open the student app and choose <strong>Sign up</strong>. You need a name, an email address
        and a password. That is all that is asked for.
      </p>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          <strong>Use your school email if you have one.</strong> If your school added you to their
          list in advance, signing up with that address links you to the school automatically.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <Image
          src={shotWelcome}
          alt="The Zengarden student app welcome screen with options to log in or sign up."
          loading="eager"
        />
        <figcaption>The welcome screen. Already have an account? Log in instead.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">2</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Join your school</h2>
      <p>
        If you were not linked automatically, your school will give you a short
        <strong>organization code</strong>. Enter it when the app asks, or later from
        <strong>My Counsellor</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Joining your school is what connects you to a counsellor and to the support your school has
        set up. Until then the app works, but it is mostly the self-guided parts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">3</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Find your way around the dashboard</h2>
      <p>Your home screen gathers everything in one place.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Next session</strong> at the top: your upcoming appointment, or a button to book
          one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pending quizzes</strong>: anything your counsellor has asked you to complete.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Resource library</strong> down the left: guided exercises, short courses and
          articles you can use on your own, any time.
        </li>
        <li><strong>My Counsellor</strong>: who you have been assigned, and how to reach them.</li>
      </ul>
      <figure>
        <Image
          src={shotHome}
          alt="The student dashboard showing a next session card with a Book a Session button, pending quizzes, a career assessment prompt, and a resource library with guided meditations."
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Everything here is yours to use whenever you want. Nothing in the resource library is
          reported to anyone.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">4</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>Meet your counsellor</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Your school assigns your counsellor</strong>, based on your class. You do not pick
        one, and you do not need to do anything to be matched.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you move class, your counsellor changes to the one assigned to your new class. If you
        would rather see someone else, that is a conversation to have with your school.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="step">
    <div class="step-number">5</div>
    <div class="step-body">
      <h2>If you need help right now</h2>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          <strong>Zengarden is not an emergency service.</strong> If you are in danger or thinking
          about harming yourself, contact emergency services on <strong>112</strong>, or
          Tele-MANAS on <strong>14416</strong>, which is free and open 24 hours. Childline on
          <strong>1098</strong> is there for anyone under 18.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        The <strong>Urgent Help</strong> panel in the app keeps these numbers one tap away from any
        screen.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-footer">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/resources/guide/student-booking">Book a session with your counsellor</a> walks
      through getting time in the diary.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/resources/guide/student-privacy">What your school can and cannot see</a> covers who
      reads what, which is worth knowing before you start writing things down.
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
